  "note": "Pins RATIFIED v1 (T-1..T-5 + constants; Xuan 2026-09-01). EXPECTED-RED: no engine implements this spec -- today generate-macros-v4/brick-workout.ts computes transition carbs as weight x 0.3/0.35 g/kg above a 180-min cliff (unratified characterization, retired by this spec); defining the published entry point (Dart mirror + edge) is part of the brick-transition bundle. engine=null until that entry point exists, like food-composition v3. BUNDLE: brick-transition (manifest at ship-bundle). Rate inputs inherit the during-workout-carbs slice (status 'recorded' there -- its own one boundary question is open and does not affect these bands). ORACLE CONVENTIONS the spec does not state: (1) rounding is half-away-from-zero; no emitted vector sits on a .5 so the convention is unchallenged by this file; (2) settle(swim)=0 -- the rate is 0 into a swim so the gap never matters; (3) a zero-intake PREVIOUS leg contributes its full duration INSTEAD OF the 15-min pre-buffer (W3's own arithmetic: 35+3+10, not 15+35+3+10). doseG is an integer by T-4 (whole grams); toleranceG kept for harness uniformity. bandLowG/bandHighG assert T-1's [0,30] on every transition. NOT COVERED (see coverage note): a raw dose landing exactly on 30 (no clean integer inputs produce it); run-ceiling effects below the clamp (mathematically unobservable in doseG: any next-run rate >70 requires mid>70, and 70 g/h over the minimum 30-min run gap already exceeds the clamp); sodium/fluid (T-5: tallies, no target -- nothing to assert numerically; the DESIGN contract TC-2/TC-4 owns their rendering).",
